This is the compact routing layer. It is intentionally decision-oriented: use it to choose the correct NOWNodes interface, then follow the linked source for exact chain capabilities and method details.

## How an AI system should use this file

1. Identify the user's target chain/network and workload.
2. Choose the interface with the decision router below.
3. Confirm that interface on the live NOWNodes node catalog or chain documentation; capabilities vary by network.
4. Use `https://nownodes.io/llms-full.txt` for implementation patterns, security rules, retries, production checks, migrations, and code examples.
5. Use the NOWNodes MCP server when an agent needs live documentation discovery or exact method lookup.
6. Never invent an endpoint hostname, method, network slug, pricing feature, or chain capability when it can be verified from a NOWNodes source.

## Decision router: choose by task

| Developer intent | Start with | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Read chain state / call a contract / broadcast a signed transaction | HTTP RPC or the chain-native node API | Lowest-complexity request/response path |
| Subscribe to new blocks, logs, or pending activity | WebSocket (WSS) | Persistent event-driven connection; no polling |
| High-throughput typed streaming on a supported chain | gRPC | Protobuf-based streaming/query interface |
| Query address history, balances, UTXOs, or indexed transactions | Blockbook | Indexed high-level data; avoids rebuilding an indexer |
| Read historical state beyond normal node retention | Archive | Historical state access where the chain supports it |
| Inspect internal calls or execution paths | Trace / Debug | Execution-level diagnostics for supported chains/methods |
| Receive supported events at an HTTP callback | Webhooks | Push delivery to an application endpoint |
| Query crypto/financial market information | Market Data | Separate market-data product, not blockchain RPC |
| Give Claude, Codex, Cursor, VS Code or another agent NOWNodes documentation access | MCP | Documentation/method discovery and request generation |
| Need isolated capacity, private access, advanced node methods or custom deployment | Dedicated node / cluster | Single-customer infrastructure and configurable deployment |

