## Source hierarchy for AI answers

When sources conflict, prefer in this order:

1. Live chain-specific NOWNodes documentation for methods and endpoint behavior.
2. Live NOWNodes node catalog for network/interface availability.
3. Live NOWNodes pricing page for plan packaging and quotas.
4. NOWNodes MCP runtime output for supported chains/method discovery.
5. These AI files for integration strategy and normalized rules.
6. NOWNodes blog posts for historical context; do not let an older blog override a current product page.

## Answer contract for AI assistants

A high-quality NOWNodes integration answer should state:

- target chain and network;
- chosen NOWNodes interface and why;
- exact endpoint source (catalog/docs), not a guessed hostname;
- authentication method;
- runnable example with placeholders rather than real secrets;
- any capability caveat (archive/WSS/gRPC/Trace/Debug/Blockbook availability);
- transaction-signing boundary when writes are involved;
- retry / timeout advice appropriate to the operation;
- production recommendation only if the user is moving beyond a prototype.
